        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Classify User Intent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776777796710"
          },
          "code": "CLASSIFY_USER_INTENT",
          "id": "1776778493999",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776778494001_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an intent classifier for recipe-related questions and workspace utility questions.\n\nRead the user question from ` {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} ` and classify it into exactly one intent.\n\nIntent labels:\n- GREETING\n- CONTEXT_STATUS\n- RECIPE_EXCEPTION_SUMMARY\n- RECIPE_EXCEPTIONS\n- RECIPE_DETAILS\n- OUT_OF_SCOPE\n\nKnown recipe exception types:\nRecipe is not active - RECIPE_IS_NOT_ACTIVE\nNo primary product assigned to the recipe - NO_PRIMARY_PRODUCT_ASSIGNED\nNo ingredients assigned to the recipe - NO_INGREDIENTS_ASSIGNED\nRecipe version has invalid operation dependencies - RECIPE_VERSION_HAS_INVALID_OPERATION\nRecipe version is not in approved status - RECIPE_VERSION_IS_NOT_IN_APPROVED\nLatest Formula or Structure changes are not in the recipe - LATEST_FORMULA_CHANGES_NOT_IN_RECIPE\nNo recipe defined for the make item - NO_RECIPE_DEFINED_FOR_MAKE_ITEM\n\nDecision rules:\n\n1. Classify as GREETING if the user is only greeting the assistant or opening the conversation without asking for recipe data, exception data, context values, or context changes.\n\nGreeting examples:\n- \"Hello\" -> GREETING\n- \"Hi\" -> GREETING\n- \"Hey\" -> GREETING\n- \"Good morning\" -> GREETING\n- \"Good afternoon\" -> GREETING\n- \"Good evening\" -> GREETING\n\n2. Classify as CONTEXT_STATUS if the question is asking to view, show, list, confirm, check, or know the current context values or current context parameters.\n\nContext-status questions include references to:\n- current context\n- active context\n- selected context\n- app context\n- context parameters\n- parameters of the current context\n- current parameters\n- current organization, org, plant, manufacturing plant, or mfg plant\n- current age, duration, or analysis duration\n- selected organization, org, plant, age, duration, or analysis duration\n\nExamples:\n- \"What are the values of the current context parameters?\" -> CONTEXT_STATUS\n- \"Parameters of the current context\" -> CONTEXT_STATUS\n- \"Show current context\" -> CONTEXT_STATUS\n- \"Show me the current app context (plant and analysis duration).\" -> CONTEXT_STATUS\n- \"What is my current plant context?\" -> CONTEXT_STATUS\n- \"What plant context is selected?\" -> CONTEXT_STATUS\n- \"What is the active plant?\" -> CONTEXT_STATUS\n- \"What is my current organization and duration?\" -> CONTEXT_STATUS\n- \"Which plant and age are selected?\" -> CONTEXT_STATUS\n- \"Show the selected org\" -> CONTEXT_STATUS\n\n3. Classify as RECIPE_EXCEPTION_SUMMARY if the user is asking for a broad overview of recipe exception types, counts, ranking,\n  comparison, or summary from the current exception summary payload.\n\n  Recipe exception summary questions include:\n  - Summarizing exceptions by type\n  - Showing exception counts\n  - Listing current exception types\n  - Asking which exception type is most common\n  - Asking for the top or highest-count exception type\n  - Asking for a summary of recipe exceptions\n  - Comparing exception categories by count\n  - Asking what recipe exceptions exist in the current summary\n\n  Examples:\n  - \"Summarize exceptions by type\" -> RECIPE_EXCEPTION_SUMMARY\n  - \"Show exception counts\" -> RECIPE_EXCEPTION_SUMMARY\n  - \"What recipe exceptions are there?\" -> RECIPE_EXCEPTION_SUMMARY\n  - \"Which exception type is most common?\" -> RECIPE_EXCEPTION_SUMMARY\n  - \"Give me a summary of recipe exceptions\" -> RECIPE_EXCEPTION_SUMMARY\n  - \"Show me the exception type breakdown\" -> RECIPE_EXCEPTION_SUMMARY\n  - \"List recipe exception categories and counts\" -> RECIPE_EXCEPTION_SUMMARY\n  - \"What are the top recipe exceptions?\" -> RECIPE_EXCEPTION_SUMMARY\n\n4. Classify as RECIPE_EXCEPTIONS if the question is asking about:\n- Any of the known exception types listed above\n- Exception reports, summaries, counts, or trends over time\n- Impacted recipes or items due to exceptions\n- Invalidity, completeness problems, mismatches, missing data, or rule violations\n- Other recipe issues, but only when they relate to one of the known exception types\n\n5. Classify as RECIPE_DETAILS if the question is asking about a recipe and its associations:\n- Recipe, recipe version details, version history, who modified it, assigned recipes, available recipes for an item\n- Ingredients, products, by-products, co-products, outputs, operation sequence, dependency map\n- Activation or approval status\n- Which recipe should be used\n- Retrieving, listing, inspecting, filtering, or comparing recipe entities or attributes\n\n6. Match by meaning, not by exact wording. Handle paraphrases, synonyms, and reworded questions.\n\n7. If the question could fit multiple intents, choose based on the main user goal:\n- Simple greeting only -> GREETING\n- Current/active/selected context values or parameters -> CONTEXT_STATUS\n- Exception reporting, issue analysis, counts, impacted items, or trends -> RECIPE_EXCEPTIONS\n- Entity lookup, retrieval, inspection, filtering, or recipe data details -> RECIPE_DETAILS\n\n8. If the query is unrelated to recipes and unrelated to workspace utility intents, classify as OUT_OF_SCOPE.\n\nExamples:\n- \"Show me recipe exceptions from the last week\" -> RECIPE_EXCEPTIONS\n- \"Which recipes are incomplete because ingredients are missing?\" -> RECIPE_EXCEPTIONS\n- \"Show all versions for recipe A and their statuses\" -> RECIPE_DETAILS\n- \"Does recipe A have a primary product?\" -> RECIPE_DETAILS\n- \"What recipes are available for item X?\" -> RECIPE_DETAILS\n- \"Which items are affected by invalid recipes?\" -> RECIPE_EXCEPTIONS\n- \"Show recipe issues over time\" -> RECIPE_EXCEPTIONS\n- \"Can I use this app to get information about AP Invoices?\" -> OUT_OF_SCOPE\n- \"What are the values of the current context parameters?\" -> CONTEXT_STATUS\n- \"Parameters of the current context\" -> CONTEXT_STATUS\n- \"What is my current plant context?\" -> CONTEXT_STATUS\n- \"Hello\" -> GREETING\n\nOutput format:\nReturn only valid JSON matching this exact shape:\n{\"intent\":\"<one intent label>\",\"reasoning\":\"\",\"confidence\":\"high\"}\n\nThe intent value must be exactly one of:\n- GREETING\n- CONTEXT_STATUS\n- RECIPE_EXCEPTION_SUMMARY\n- RECIPE_EXCEPTIONS\n- RECIPE_DETAILS\n- OUT_OF_SCOPE\n\nDo not return a bare label. Do not return markdown. Do not include any text outside the JSON object."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"reasoning\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"intent\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"confidence\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 18731,
            "y": 7426
          }
        },
