        {
          "metadata": {
            "agentCode": "ORA_PROC_MFG_RECIPE_QUERY_ANALYST",
            "description": "The Process Manufacturing Recipe Agent supports the retrieval of process manufacturing work definitions within Oracle SCM. The agent supports the following core functions:\n\n- Retrieve Recipe/Work Definition Details: Given search criteria or a recipe name, the agent fetches comprehensive details such as operations, versions, material, outputs and related data.\n\nThis tool enhances efficiency in searching for specific process manufacturing recipes/work definitions, supporting operational needs.",
            "name": "Get Recipe Details Query",
            "type": "REUSABLE"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GET_RECIPE_DETAILS_QUERY",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1776777861032",
          "id": "1776773387474",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776774738436_1",
              "name": "message",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1776774738438_2",
              "name": "pAge",
              "type": "integer",
              "value": "{{$context.$variables.age}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1776774738439_3",
              "name": "pOrganizationId",
              "type": "integer",
              "value": "{{$context.$variables.organizationId}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": " ",
          "type": "AGENT",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 17582,
            "y": 7870
          }
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "SOURCE_WORKER_OUTPUT:\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_RECIPE_DETAILS_SUMMARY.$output.result}}\n\nCURRENT_USER_MESSAGE:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nYou are formatting the final response for Oracle SCM recipe exception details.\n\nUse only SOURCE_WORKER_OUTPUT as source data.\n\nCritical rules:\n- Never invent records.\n- Never create sample rows.\n- Never use placeholder values such as Process 1, Recipe 1, Product A, Type X, v1.0, Pending, Draft, or any similar demo data.\n- The examples in the system/widget documentation are formatting examples only. They are not data.\n- If a value does not appear in SOURCE_WORKER_OUTPUT, do not output it.\n- If SOURCE_WORKER_OUTPUT is null, empty, unavailable, or does not contain record values, do not create recipe rows.\n- If no actual exception records are found, do not output oraInfoDisplay and do not output multiRecordWidget.\n- Do not use general knowledge to add causes, reasons, risks, or resolution steps.\n- All final response content must be grounded in SOURCE_WORKER_OUTPUT.\n\nRecord extraction:\nExtract only explicit record fields from SOURCE_WORKER_OUTPUT.\n\nSupported record fields:\n- Process\n- Recipe\n- Product\n- User Item Type\n- Recipe Quantity\n- Batch Quantity\n- Version\n- Version Status\n- Recipe Status\n- Start Date\n\nProduct-only records may appear as:\nProduct: <value>, User Item Type: <value>\n\nRecipe detail records may appear as:\nProcess: <value>\nRecipe: <value>\nProduct: <value>\nUser Item Type: <value>\nRecipe Quantity: <value>\nRecipe Status: <value>\nVersion: <value>\nVersion Status: <value>\nStart Date: <value>\n\nStart Date formatting:\n- When displaying Start Date in the multiRecordWidget, convert ISO timestamp values to `Mon DD YYYY HH:MI AM/PM`.\n- Example: `2026-05-26T10:46:01+00:00` should be displayed as `May 26 2026 10:46 AM`.\n- Example: `2026-04-28T06:16:01+00:00` should be displayed as `Apr 28 2026 06:16 AM`.\n- Use three-letter English month abbreviations with first letter capitalized, such as `Jan`, `Feb`, `Mar`, `Apr`, `May`.\n- Use 12-hour time with uppercase `AM` or `PM`.\n- Do not display seconds.\n- Do not adjust or convert the timezone. Use the date and time components from the source value.\n- If Start Date is blank, null, missing, or unavailable, leave the Start Date value blank.\n- Do not change or infer any other date/time value.\n\nNo-record handling:\n- If SOURCE_WORKER_OUTPUT says no records are available, no details were returned, no matching records exist, or there are no recipe exception detail records, return only the no-record message and guidance found in SOURCE_WORKER_OUTPUT.\n- Do not create an oraInfoDisplay.\n- Do not create a multiRecordWidget.\n- Do not create a one-row Message table.\n- Do not add duplicate wording.\n- Do not add additional possible reasons or resolution steps that are not present in SOURCE_WORKER_OUTPUT.\n\nRecord output format:\n- If actual records are found, output the multiRecordWidget first inside an oraInfoDisplay XML tag.\n- After the widget, include only non-record guidance from SOURCE_WORKER_OUTPUT as a bulleted list.\n- Do not repeat record details after the widget.\n\nWidget rules:\n- Use patternId: multiRecordWidget.\n- Use key: list.\n- Use title: Recipe Exception Details.\n- Use description based on the exception name when available in SOURCE_WORKER_OUTPUT.\n- Use properties.subtitle to describe the records briefly.\n- Use only columns that have at least one nonblank value in extracted records.\n- Preserve this column order when present:\n  1. Process\n  2. Recipe\n  3. Product\n  4. User Item Type\n  5. Batch Quantity\n  6. Version\n  7. Version Status\n  8. Recipe Status\n  9. Start Date\n- Map Recipe Quantity to Batch Quantity.\n- Each row must represent one extracted source record.\n- Do not combine Product and User Item Type into one value.\n- Limit to 10 rows unless SOURCE_WORKER_OUTPUT says the user explicitly requested more.\n\nGuidance rules:\n- Always format non-record guidance as a bulleted list.\n- Use only guidance statements that already appear in SOURCE_WORKER_OUTPUT.\n- You may split long SOURCE_WORKER_OUTPUT sentences into clearer bullets.\n- You may lightly rephrase SOURCE_WORKER_OUTPUT guidance for clarity, but do not add new meaning.\n- Do not make the guidance more elaborate than SOURCE_WORKER_OUTPUT.\n- Do not introduce new causes, reasons, solutions, risks, validations, approvals, dependencies, or operational steps.\n- Use CURRENT_USER_MESSAGE only to decide which SOURCE_WORKER_OUTPUT guidance sections are relevant and how to label them.\n- If the user asks for possible reasons and SOURCE_WORKER_OUTPUT contains reason/cause guidance, include a bullet section titled `Possible reasons:`.\n- If the user asks for resolution, fix, steps, or actions and SOURCE_WORKER_OUTPUT contains resolution guidance, include a bullet section titled `Recommended resolution steps:`.\n- If SOURCE_WORKER_OUTPUT does not include possible reasons, do not create a `Possible reasons:` section.\n- If SOURCE_WORKER_OUTPUT does not include resolution steps, do not create a `Recommended resolution steps:` section.\n- Do not ask follow-up questions at the end.\n- Do not use paragraphs for guidance after the widget; use bullets only.\n\nDo not output:\n- Raw JSON outside oraInfoDisplay\n- Markdown tables\n- HTML tables\n- Demo data\n- Placeholder records\n- Message-only widgets\n- Duplicate record details\n- Generated using...\n- Explanation of how the data was transformed\n- Any guidance not grounded in SOURCE_WORKER_OUTPUT"
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "agentCode": "ORA_RECIPE_EXCEPTION_DETAILS_QUERY_ANALYST",
            "description": "The Process Manufacturing Recipe Exception Details Query Analyst1 retrieves process manufacturing recipe and work definition details in Oracle SCM. It supports exception-based lookup of recipes/work definitions by category, returning the list of records associated with the specified exception so users can quickly identify items that require review, audit, or corrective action.\n\nCore capability:\n- Retrieve Recipe/Work Definition Details: Given a valid exception category, the agent fetches the matching recipe details for analysis and operational follow-up.\n\nThis improves efficiency when searching for process manufacturing recipes/work definitions and supports operational oversight and compliance activities.",
            "name": "Get Recipe Details Summary",
            "type": "REUSABLE"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GET_RECIPE_DETAILS_SUMMARY",
          "id": "1776779458964",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776779474905_1",
              "name": "message",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1776779474906_2",
              "name": "pOrganizationId",
              "type": "integer",
              "value": "{{$context.$variables.organizationId}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1776779474907_3",
              "name": "pAge",
              "type": "integer",
              "value": "{{$context.$variables.age}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": " ",
          "type": "AGENT",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 18032,
            "y": 7870
          }
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
