          "metadata": {
            "name": "Recipe is not active"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "RECIPE_IS_NOT_ACTIVE",
          "id": "1775324846897",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775324846898_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "From {{$context.$variables.RecipeDetailsArray}} , analyze the records and generate a data-driven description under 100 words for a Supply Chain Process Manufacturing Production Supervisor or Plant Engineer. Base the description only on the records provided. Summarize the key operational issue, affected processes/recipes/products, inactive recipe or version status patterns, production readiness impact, and the most important next action. Use a practical, plant-floor decision-support tone focused on recipe activation, release readiness, scheduling risk, and master data governance.\n\nThen extract the following fields for each record:\n- Process\n- Recipe\n- VersionNumber\n- StartDate\n- Product\n- UserItemType\n- RecipeQuantity\n- VersionStatus\n- RecipeStatus\n- WorkDefinitionId (THIS IS ONLY USED FOR THE ACTIONS INSIDE EACH ROW, NOT FOR DISPLAYING)\n\nDisplay the results using a multiRecordWidget with the following columns and exact order:\n\n1. Process → Process Name\n2. Recipe → Recipe\n3. VersionNumber → Version\n4. StartDate → Start Date\n5. Product → Product\n6. UserItemType → User Item Type\n7. RecipeQuantity → Batch Quantity\n8. VersionStatus → Version Status\n9. RecipeStatus → Recipe Status\n\nSet the multiRecordWidget Subject property as:\n\"Recipe is not active\"\n\n#ACTION\n\nFor each row in `multiRecordWidget`, inspect the value of `RecipeStatus`.\n\nIf `RecipeStatus` is `Inactive`, generate an actionable insight with the following values:\n\ntitle: \"Reactivate\"\nactionText: \"Reactivate\"\nshortDescription: \"Change the recipe status from Inactive to Activate\"\nfollowUpCommand: ora.Invoke(RefreshRecipeExceptions,{\"command\": \"activate\",\"WorkDefinitionId\":<WorkDefinitionId>,\"Recipe\":<Recipe>,\"Process\":<Process>,\"VersionNumber\":\"1\"})\n\nWhere <WorkDefinitionId> is the value you extracted from the array for that specific row\n\nStart Date formatting:\n- Convert StartDate from ISO timestamp format to `DD-Mon-YYYY`.\n- Example: `2026-05-26T10:46:01+00:00` should be displayed as `26-May-2026`.\n- Example: `2026-04-28T06:16:01+00:00` should be displayed as `28-May-2026`.\n- Use three-letter English month abbreviations with first letter capitalized, such as `Jan`, `Feb`, `Mar`, `Apr`, `May`.\n- Do not display seconds.\n- If StartDate is blank, null, missing, or unavailable, leave the Start Date value blank.\n- Do not change or infer any other date/time value.\n\nEnsure:\n- Each row represents one record from the source data.\n- Include the generated description and the multiRecordWidget in the output.\n- Do not display raw JSON, explanations, or instructions.\n- Preserve the exact column order specified above."
            }
          ],
