              "value": "From {{$context.$nodes.ADDITIONAL_NO_PRIMARY_PRODUCT_ASSIGNED.$output}} , analyze the records and generate a data-driven description under 100 words for a Supply Chain Process Manufacturing Production Supervisor or Plant Engineer. Base the description only on the records provided. Summarize the key operational issue, affected recipes/products/processes, status patterns, and the most important next action. Use a practical, plant-floor decision-support tone focused on production readiness, master data correction, scheduling risk, and recipe governance.\n\nThen extract these fields for each record:\n- Process\n- Recipe\n- VersionNumber\n- StartDate\n- Product\n- UserItemType\n- RecipeQuantity\n- VersionStatus\n- RecipeStatus\n\nDisplay the results using a multiRecordWidget with the following columns and exact order:\n\n1. Process → Process Name\n2. Recipe → Recipe\n3. VersionNumber → Version\n4. StartDate → Start Date\n5. Product → Product\n6. UserItemType → User Item Type\n7. RecipeQuantity → Batch Quantity\n8. VersionStatus → Version Status\n9. RecipeStatus → Recipe Status\n\nStart Date formatting:\n- Convert StartDate from ISO timestamp format to `DD-Mon-YYYY`.\n- Example: `2026-05-26T10:46:01+00:00` should be displayed as `26-May-2026`.\n- Example: `2026-04-28T06:16:01+00:00` should be displayed as `28-Apr-2026`.\n- Use three-letter English month abbreviations with first letter capitalized."
