          "code": "GENERATE_EMAIL_CONTENT",
          "id": "1781503459714",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1781503459715_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Fill only the communication parameters listed in {{$context.$app.$OraCommParamsToFill}}.\n\nUse these parameter values:\nPlantName = {{$context.$variables.organizationCode}}\nAge = {{$context.$variables.age}}\nUserName = {{$context.$user.$name}}\n\nUse this source data for recipe exceptions:\n{{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_RECIPE_EXCEPTION_DATA.$output}}\n\nParameter mapping rules:\n\n1. RecipeExceptionData\n- Read the source data from {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_RECIPE_EXCEPTION_DATA.$output}}.\n- Skip any exception record that is null, empty, undefined, or does not contain usable exception data.\n- Ignore ExceptionCode.\n- For each valid exception record, extract only:\n  - ExceptionMessage\n  - ExceptionCount\n- Map each valid record to this shape:\n  {\n    \"Exceptions\": ExceptionMessage,\n    \"Count\": ExceptionCount\n  }\n- Preserve Count as a number.\n\n2. RecipeExceptionSummaryData\nGenerate one concise operational summary from the same source data.\n\n- If there are no valid source records, or all valid records have ExceptionCount equal to 0, null, empty, or undefined, set RecipeExceptionSummaryData to:\n\"No recipe exceptions require supervisor or production engineering attention at this time.\"\n\n- If any valid record has a non-zero ExceptionCount, write one summary under 60 words.\n- Use only ExceptionMessage and ExceptionCount from the source records.\n- Identify the highest-count or highest-impact exception.\n- Mention total exception pressure where useful.\n- Include practical next steps.\n- Use a production supervisor or manufacturing engineer tone.\n\nGlobal rules:\n1. Fill only parameters present in {{$context.$app.$OraCommParamsToFill}}.\n2. Preserve Age and Count as numbers.\n3. Do not include null, empty, or undefined exception records in RecipeExceptionData.\n4. Do not use or return ExceptionCode.\n5. Return only the FillParameters output.\n6. Do not include markdown, explanations, comments, or extra text."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 20828,
            "y": 7426
          }
        },
